  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1: Feasibility and Zoning Check. Before anything else, we'll assess your property to confirm it's suitable for a granny flat. This involves checking local zoning regulations, understanding setback requirements in your specific city (like Berkeley or San Leandro), and looking at existing structures and utility connections. This initial step helps us understand what's possible and what limitations might exist.",
      "text": "Step 1: Feasibility and Zoning Check. Before anything else, we'll assess your property to confirm it's suitable for a granny flat. This involves checking local zoning regulations, understanding setback requirements in your specific city (like Berkeley or San Leandro), and looking at existing structures and utility connections. This initial step helps us understand what's possible and what limitations might exist."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Step 2: Design and Planning. This is where your vision starts to take shape! We'll work with designers and engineers to create architectural and structural plans. This includes floor plans, elevations, utility designs (water, sewer, electrical), and drainage plans. For properties with challenging topography, like some in the Oakland Hills, this stage will involve specialized engineering to ensure structural integrity.",
      "text": "Step 2: Design and Planning. This is where your vision starts to take shape! We'll work with designers and engineers to create architectural and structural plans. This includes floor plans, elevations, utility designs (water, sewer, electrical), and drainage plans. For properties with challenging topography, like some in the Oakland Hills, this stage will involve specialized engineering to ensure structural integrity."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "Step 3: Permit Application and Approval. Once designs are finalized, we prepare and submit all necessary planning and building permit applications to your local jurisdiction. This can be a complex phase, navigating various departmental requirements. We manage this process, aiming for efficient approval, though actual timing can vary depending on city workload.",
      "text": "Step 3: Permit Application and Approval. Once designs are finalized, we prepare and submit all necessary planning and building permit applications to your local jurisdiction. This can be a complex phase, navigating various departmental requirements. We manage this process, aiming for efficient approval, though actual timing can vary depending on city workload."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4,
      "name": "Step 4: Site Preparation and Foundation. With permits in hand, construction begins! This involves preparing the site, which could include clearing, grading, and ensuring proper drainage. Then, the foundation is laid, which is critical for the stability of your new unit. For any new structure, especially detached units, a robust foundation is essential.",
      "text": "Step 4: Site Preparation and Foundation. With permits in hand, construction begins! This involves preparing the site, which could include clearing, grading, and ensuring proper drainage. Then, the foundation is laid, which is critical for the stability of your new unit. For any new structure, especially detached units, a robust foundation is essential."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5,
      "name": "Step 5: Framing, Roofing, and Utilities. Next comes the framing – erecting the skeleton of your granny flat. Once the framing is complete and passed inspection, the roof is installed, making the structure weather-tight. Concurrently, rough-ins for electrical wiring, plumbing, and HVAC systems are installed, ready for connection.",
      "text": "Step 5: Framing, Roofing, and Utilities. Next comes the framing – erecting the skeleton of your granny flat. Once the framing is complete and passed inspection, the roof is installed, making the structure weather-tight. Concurrently, rough-ins for electrical wiring, plumbing, and HVAC systems are installed, ready for connection."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 6,
      "name": "Step 6: Exterior and Interior Finishes. This is where it really starts to look like a home! Exterior work includes siding, windows, and doors. Inside, we install insulation, drywall, flooring, custom cabinetry, countertops, and all the fixtures and finishes you’ve chosen. Every detail is brought together to create a cohesive and functional living space.",
      "text": "Step 6: Exterior and Interior Finishes. This is where it really starts to look like a home! Exterior work includes siding, windows, and doors. Inside, we install insulation, drywall, flooring, custom cabinetry, countertops, and all the fixtures and finishes you’ve chosen. Every detail is brought together to create a cohesive and functional living space."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 7,
      "name": "Step 7: Final Inspections and Occupancy. Before you can officially use your new granny flat, it must pass final inspections from the building department. Once approved, we obtain the necessary occupancy or use approval. We handle these final steps, ensuring everything is compliant and ready for your family or tenants. Hometelligent Inc. prides itself on meticulous execution and communication throughout every phase, ensuring your project goes smoothly from start to finish. We’ve been transforming East Bay homes with ADUs and additions since 1993, building relationships along the way.",
      "text": "What to Do Next Ready to add a granny flat to your property? Understanding this process is the first step. For a personalized assessment and to discuss how Hometelligent Inc. can manage your project with expertise and care, contact us today for a consultation."
    }
  ],
